  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Fedex Supply Chain Distribution System recorded $86.3M in contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The vendor won 15 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $5.8M. Obligations are down 78.9% year over year compared with prior periods. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer so far, accounting for $86.3M in obligations. Historical obligations show a multi-year rise from $253M in FY22 to $409M in FY26, followed by the current-year total of $86.3M. The Department of Justice appears as a secondary buyer with $15K in obligations. These figures are contract obligations unless noted otherwise for award values or total contract values.",
